IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc18-soira-notice`

-- ccc18-soira-foreign.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 490.02901 to 490.02911 (notice and obligation to comply with the
-- Sex Offender Information Registration Act: convictions outside Canada, Form 54). Part agent ccc18; layer 1. It imports `ccc18-soira-notice` for the
-- maximum-term bands and the end-of-obligation type, which sections 490.02904, 490.02908 and 490.02912 use again. Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE of a type):
-- JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words), NOTHING (not covered); see the header of `ccc18-soira-notice` and NOTES.md.

§ `Sections 490.02901 to 490.02911 -- Notice and obligation to comply: convictions outside Canada`

§ `490.02901 Obligation`

-- src:10379 | Notice and Obligation to Comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act — Convictions Outside Canada
-- src:10380 | Obligation
-- src:10381 | 490.02901 A person who is served with a notice in Form 54 shall comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act for the applicable period specified in section 490.02904 unless a court makes an exemption order under subsection 490.02905(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02901 (src:10379-10381)
DECLARE `s 490.02901 action` IS ONE OF `s 490.02901 comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act for the applicable period specified in section 490.02904`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02901 (src:10379-10381)
GIVEN `the person is served with a notice in Form 54` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court makes an exemption order under subsection 490.02905(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02901 the person shall comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` MEANS
    IF `a court makes an exemption order under subsection 490.02905(2)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act for the applicable period specified in section 490.02904 unless a court makes an exemption order under subsection 490.02905(2)"
    ELSE IF `the person is served with a notice in Form 54`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid on "A person who is served with a notice in Form 54"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02901 (src:10379-10381)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.02901 action`
`s 490.02901 the duty of the offender to comply` MEANS
    PARTY `the offender`
    MUST `s 490.02901 comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act for the applicable period specified in section 490.02904`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the offender` BECAUSE "the person did not comply with the Sex Offender Information Registration Act"

§ `490.02902 Persons who may be served`

-- src:10382 | Persons who may be served
-- src:10383 | 490.02902 (1) The Attorney General of a province, or the minister of justice of a territory, may serve a person with a notice in Form 54 only if the person arrived in Canada on or after April 15, 2011 and they were convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for an offence outside Canada — other than a service offence as defined in subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act — that is, in the opinion of the Attorney General or minister of justice, equivalent to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02902(1) (src:10382-10383)
GIVEN `the day on which the person arrived in Canada` IS A DATE
      `they were convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for an offence outside Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is a service offence as defined in subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Attorney General or minister of justice, the offence is equivalent to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02902(1) the Attorney General or minister of justice may serve the person with a notice in Form 54` MEANS
    IF `the day on which the person arrived in Canada` AT LEAST Date 15 4 2011
       AND `they were convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for an offence outside Canada`
       AND (NOT `the offence is a service offence as defined in subsection 2(1) of the National Defence Act`)
       AND `in the opinion of the Attorney General or minister of justice, the offence is equivalent to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may serve a person with a notice in Form 54 only if the person arrived in Canada on or after April 15, 2011"

-- src:10384 | Exception
-- src:10385 | (2) The notice shall not be served on a person who has been acquitted of every offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.02903.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02902(2) (src:10384-10385)
GIVEN `the person has been acquitted of every offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.02903` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02902(2) a notice shall not be served on the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has been acquitted of every offence in connection with which a notice may be served on them under section 490.02903`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies: "The notice shall not be served on a person who has been acquitted"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is limited to a person acquitted of every such offence

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02902(2) (src:10384-10385)
GIVEN `the answer of s 490.02902(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 490.02902(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02902 the notice in Form 54 may be served, subject to subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 490.02902(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice shall not be served on a person who has been acquitted of every offence"
    ELSE `the answer of s 490.02902(1)`

§ `490.02903 Period for and method of service; proof of service`

-- src:10386 | Period for and method of service
-- src:10387 | 490.02903 (1) A notice in Form 54 shall be personally served.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02903(1) (src:10386-10387)
GIVEN `the notice is personally served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02903(1) the manner of service is the one the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice is personally served` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A notice in Form 54 shall be personally served"

-- src:10388 | Proof of service
-- src:10389 | (2) An affidavit of the person who served the notice, sworn before a commissioner or other person authorized to take affidavits, is evidence of the service and the notice if it sets out that
-- src:10390 | (a) the person who served the notice has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case;
-- src:10391 | (b) the notice was personally served on the person to whom it was directed on a named day; and
-- src:10392 | (c) the person who served the notice identifies a true copy of the notice as an exhibit attached to the affidavit.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02903(2) (src:10388-10392)
GIVEN `it is an affidavit of the person who served the notice, sworn before a commissioner or other person authorized to take affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) it sets out that the person who served the notice has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) it sets out that the notice was personally served on the person to whom it was directed on a named day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) it sets out that the person who served the notice identifies a true copy of the notice as an exhibit attached to the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02903(2) the affidavit is evidence of the service and the notice` MEANS
    IF `it is an affidavit of the person who served the notice, sworn before a commissioner or other person authorized to take affidavits`
       AND `(a) it sets out that the person who served the notice has charge of the appropriate records and has knowledge of the facts in the particular case`
       AND `(b) it sets out that the notice was personally served on the person to whom it was directed on a named day`
       AND `(c) it sets out that the person who served the notice identifies a true copy of the notice as an exhibit attached to the affidavit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is evidence of the service and the notice if it sets out that" [marginal (a)]

-- src:10393 | Requirements relating to notice
-- src:10394 | (3) The person who served the notice shall, without delay, send a copy of the affidavit and the notice to the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the person was served.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02903(3) (src:10393-10394)
DECLARE `s 490.02903(3) party` IS ONE OF `s 490.02903(3) the person who served the notice`   -- not in the core's Party: NEEDS-CORE.md
DECLARE `s 490.02903(3) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.02903(3) send a copy of the affidavit and the notice to the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the person was served`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02903(3) (src:10393-10394)
GIVEN `they served the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02903(3) the person who served the notice must send a copy of the affidavit and the notice` MEANS
    IF `they served the notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "The person who served the notice shall, without delay"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02903(3) (src:10393-10394)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 490.02903(3) party` `s 490.02903(3) action`
`s 490.02903(3) the duty of the person who served the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `s 490.02903(3) the person who served the notice`
    MUST `s 490.02903(3) send a copy of the affidavit and the notice to the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the person was served`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 490.02903(3) the person who served the notice` BECAUSE "the copy of the affidavit and the notice was not sent to the Attorney General or minister of justice"

§ `490.02904 When obligation begins; when obligation ends; duration of obligation`

-- src:10395 | When obligation begins
-- src:10396 | 490.02904 (1) The obligation under section 490.02901 begins on the day on which the person is served with the notice.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02904(1) (src:10395-10396)
GIVEN `the day on which the person is served with the notice` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 490.02904(1) the day on which the obligation under section 490.02901 begins` MEANS `the day on which the person is served with the notice`

-- src:10397 | When obligation ends
-- src:10398 | (2) The obligation ends on the day on which an exemption order is made.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02904(2) (src:10397-10398)
GIVEN `the day on which an exemption order is made, if one is` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 490.02904(2) the day on which the obligation ends` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which an exemption order is made, if one is`
    WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The obligation ends on the day on which an exemption order is made"; with no exemption order, subsection (3) governs

-- src:10399 | Duration of obligation
-- src:10400 | (3) If subsection (2) does not apply, the obligation
-- src:10401 | (a) ends 10 years after the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder if the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence is two or five years;
-- src:10402 | (b) ends 20 years after the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder if the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence is 10 or 14 years;
-- src:10403 | (c) applies for life if the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence is life; or
-- src:10404 | (d) applies for life if, on April 15, 2011 or before or after that day, the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, more than one offence outside Canada that is, in the opinion of the Attorney General of the province or minister of justice of the territory, equivalent to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1) and if more than one of those offences is listed in the notice.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02904(3) (src:10399-10404)
GIVEN `the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the day on which the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A DATE
      `(d) on April 15, 2011 or before or after that day, the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, more than one offence outside Canada that is, in the opinion of the Attorney General of the province or minister of justice of the territory, equivalent to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(d) more than one of those offences is listed in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation`
`s 490.02904(3) the obligation, if subsection (2) does not apply, ends or applies for life` MEANS
    IF `(d) on April 15, 2011 or before or after that day, the person was convicted of, or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for, more than one offence outside Canada that is, in the opinion of the Attorney General of the province or minister of justice of the territory, equivalent to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1)`
       AND `(d) more than one of those offences is listed in the notice`
    THEN JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life`   -- paragraph (d)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 490.022(3) the band of the maximum term of imprisonment` `the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence`
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of two or five years` THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (`s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` 10))   -- paragraph (a)
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of 10 or 14 years` THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (`s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` 20))   -- paragraph (b)
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of life` THEN JUST `s 490.022(3) applies for life`   -- paragraph (c)
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) any other maximum term, or none stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names maximum terms of two, five, 10, 14 years and life only

§ `490.02905 Application for exemption order`

-- src:10405 | Application for exemption order
-- src:10406 | 490.02905 (1) A person who is served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903 may apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction for an order exempting them from the obligation within one year after they are served.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(1) (src:10405-10406)
GIVEN `they are served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which they were served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply for an order exempting them from the obligation` IS A DATE
      `the application is made to a court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02905(1) the person may apply for an exemption order` MEANS
    IF NOT `they are served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903 may apply"
    ELSE IF `the day on which they apply for an order exempting them from the obligation` LESS THAN `the day on which they were served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903` OR `the day on which they apply for an order exempting them from the obligation` GREATER THAN `s 490.021(1) one year after the day` `the day on which they were served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction for an order exempting them from the obligation within one year after they are served"
         ELSE IF `the application is made to a court of criminal jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is to apply "to a court of criminal jurisdiction"

-- src:10407 | Exemption order
-- src:10408 | (2) The court shall make an exemption order if it is satisfied that the person has established that
-- src:10409 | (a) they were not convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for or were acquitted of the offence in question;
-- src:10410 | (b) the offence in question is not equivalent to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1);
-- src:10411 | (c) there is no connection between the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act; or
-- src:10412 | (d) the impact of the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, is grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(2) (src:10407-10412)
DECLARE `s 490.02905(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.02905(2) make an exemption order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(2) (src:10407-10412)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the person has established that they were not convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for or were acquitted of the offence in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the offence in question is not equivalent to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has established that there is no connection between the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, is grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02905(2) the court shall make an exemption order` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that they were not convicted of or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder for or were acquitted of the offence in question`
       OR `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the offence in question is not equivalent to an offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1)`
       OR `the court is satisfied that the person has established that there is no connection between the obligation and the purpose of helping police services prevent or investigate crimes of a sexual nature by requiring the registration of information relating to sex offenders under the Sex Offender Information Registration Act`
       OR `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the impact of the obligation on the person, including on their privacy or liberty, is grossly disproportionate to the public interest in protecting society through the effective prevention or investigation of crimes of a sexual nature, to be achieved by the registration of information relating to sex offenders under that Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall make an exemption order if it is satisfied that the person has established that" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(2) (src:10407-10412)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.02905(2) action`
`s 490.02905(2) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.02905(2) make an exemption order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of a ground and did not make an exemption order"

-- src:10413 | Factors
-- src:10414 | (2.1) In determining whether to make an exemption order under paragraph (2)(c) or (d), the court shall consider
-- src:10415 | (a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation;
-- src:10416 | (b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics;
-- src:10417 | (c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim;
-- src:10418 | (d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person;
-- src:10419 | (e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence;
-- src:10420 | (f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person; and
-- src:10421 | (g) any other factors that the court considers relevant.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(2.1) (src:10413-10421)
DECLARE `s 490.02905(2.1) factor` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.02905(2.1)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation`
    `s 490.02905(2.1)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics`
    `s 490.02905(2.1)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim`
    `s 490.02905(2.1)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person`
    `s 490.02905(2.1)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence`
    `s 490.02905(2.1)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person`
    `s 490.02905(2.1)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant`
    `s 490.02905(2.1) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(2.1) (src:10413-10421)
GIVEN `the court is determining whether to make an exemption order under paragraph (2)(c) or (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      factor IS A `s 490.02905(2.1) factor`
      `the court considers the matter relevant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02905(2.1) the court shall consider the factor` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court is determining whether to make an exemption order under paragraph (2)(c) or (d)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In determining whether to make an exemption order under paragraph (2)(c) or (d), the court shall consider" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE CONSIDER factor
         WHEN `s 490.02905(2.1)(a) the nature and seriousness of the offence that is the basis of the obligation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02905(2.1)(b) the victim’s age and other personal characteristics` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02905(2.1)(c) the nature and circumstances of the relationship between the person and the victim` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02905(2.1)(d) the personal characteristics and circumstances of the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02905(2.1)(e) the person’s criminal history, including the age at which they previously committed any offence and the length of time for which they have been at liberty without committing an offence` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02905(2.1)(f) the opinions of experts who have examined the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 490.02905(2.1)(g) any other factors that the court considers relevant` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (g): "any other factors that the court considers relevant" is itself in the list
         WHEN `s 490.02905(2.1) a matter outside paragraphs (a) to (f)` THEN IF `the court considers the matter relevant` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): only factors "that the court considers relevant" are added by paragraph (g)

-- src:10422 | Order to correct
-- src:10423 | (2.2) If the court does not make an exemption order but is satisfied that the offence in question, though not equivalent to the offence referred to in the notice, is equivalent to another offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1), the court shall order that the notice be corrected.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(2.2) (src:10422-10423)
DECLARE `s 490.02905(2.2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.02905(2.2) order that the notice be corrected`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(2.2) (src:10422-10423)
GIVEN `the court does not make an exemption order but is satisfied that the offence in question, though not equivalent to the offence referred to in the notice, is equivalent to another offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02905(2.2) the court shall order that the notice be corrected` MEANS
    IF `the court does not make an exemption order but is satisfied that the offence in question, though not equivalent to the offence referred to in the notice, is equivalent to another offence referred to in paragraph (a) of the definition primary offence in subsection 490.011(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court does not make an exemption order but is satisfied that the offence in question" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(2.2) (src:10422-10423)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.02905(2.2) action`
`s 490.02905(2.2) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.02905(2.2) order that the notice be corrected`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of the equivalence to another offence and did not order that the notice be corrected"

-- src:10424 | Reasons for decision
-- src:10425 | (3) The court shall give reasons for its decision.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(3) (src:10424-10425)
DECLARE `s 490.02905(3) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.02905(3) give reasons for its decision`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(3) (src:10424-10425)
GIVEN `the court has made a decision under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02905(3) the court shall give reasons for its decision` MEANS
    IF `the court has made a decision under this section` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "The court shall give reasons for its decision"

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(3) (src:10424-10425)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.02905(3) action`
`s 490.02905(3) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.02905(3) give reasons for its decision`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not give reasons for its decision"

-- src:10426 | Removal of information from database
-- src:10427 | (4) If the court makes an exemption order, it shall also make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of the copy of the notice.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(4) (src:10426-10427)
DECLARE `s 490.02905(4) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.02905(4) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of the copy of the notice`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(4) (src:10426-10427)
GIVEN `the court makes an exemption order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02905(4) the court shall also make an order for removal of the information from the database` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an exemption order` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the court makes an exemption order" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02905(4) (src:10426-10427)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 490.02905(4) action`
`s 490.02905(4) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.02905(4) make an order requiring the Royal Canadian Mounted Police to permanently remove from the database all information that relates to the person that was registered in the database on receipt of the copy of the notice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made an exemption order and did not order the removal of the information"

