§ `490.029051 Application for variation order`

-- src:10430 | Application for variation order
-- src:10431 | 490.029051 (1) A person who is served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903 may, within one year after they are served, apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction for an order to vary the duration of the obligation if
-- src:10432 | (a) the obligation applies for life under paragraph 490.02904(3)(d); and
-- src:10433 | (b) none of the offences in question listed in the notice have an equivalent offence with a maximum term of imprisonment for life provided for in Canadian law.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029051(1) (src:10430-10433)
GIVEN `they are served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which they were served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903` IS A DATE
      `the day on which they apply for an order to vary the duration of the obligation` IS A DATE
      `the application is made to a court of criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) the obligation applies for life under paragraph 490.02904(3)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) none of the offences in question listed in the notice have an equivalent offence with a maximum term of imprisonment for life provided for in Canadian law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029051(1) the person may apply for a variation order` MEANS
    IF NOT `they are served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who is served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903 may"
    ELSE IF `the day on which they apply for an order to vary the duration of the obligation` LESS THAN `the day on which they were served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903` OR `the day on which they apply for an order to vary the duration of the obligation` GREATER THAN `s 490.021(1) one year after the day` `the day on which they were served with a notice in Form 54 under section 490.02903`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, within one year after they are served, apply to a court of criminal jurisdiction for an order to vary the duration of the obligation"
         ELSE IF `the application is made to a court of criminal jurisdiction`
                 AND `(a) the obligation applies for life under paragraph 490.02904(3)(d)`
                 AND `(b) none of the offences in question listed in the notice have an equivalent offence with a maximum term of imprisonment for life provided for in Canadian law`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is given "if (a) the obligation applies for life under paragraph 490.02904(3)(d); and (b) none of the offences in question"

-- src:10434 | Variation order
-- src:10435 | (2) The court shall make the variation order if it is satisfied that the person has established that the offences in question listed in the notice do not demonstrate, or do not form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029051(2) (src:10434-10435)
DECLARE `s 490.029051(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.029051(2) make the variation order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029051(2) (src:10434-10435)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the offences in question listed in the notice do not demonstrate, or do not form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.029051(2) the court shall make the variation order` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the person has established that the offences in question listed in the notice do not demonstrate, or do not form part of, a pattern of behaviour showing that the person presents an increased risk of reoffending by committing a crime of a sexual nature`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall make the variation order if it is satisfied that the person has established that the offences in question" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029051(2) (src:10434-10435)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.029051(2) action`
`s 490.029051(2) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.029051(2) make the variation order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of the ground and did not make the variation order"

-- src:10436 | Variation of duration
-- src:10437 | (3) If the court makes a variation order, it shall set out the duration of the obligation in the order, which shall be determined by applying paragraphs 490.02904(3)(a) and (b) to the offence in question listed in the notice whose equivalent offence has the longest maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law.
@ref Criminal Code s 490.029051(3) (src:10436-10437)
GIVEN `the court makes a variation order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence that has the longest maximum term, of the offences in question listed in the notice` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the day on which the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for that offence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 490.022(3) end of the obligation`
`s 490.029051(3) the duration of the obligation set out in the variation order` MEANS
    IF NOT `the court makes a variation order`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court makes a variation order, it shall set out the duration of the obligation in the order"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 490.022(3) the band of the maximum term of imprisonment` `the maximum term of imprisonment provided for in Canadian law for the equivalent offence that has the longest maximum term, of the offences in question listed in the notice`
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of two or five years` THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (`s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for that offence` 10))   -- paragraph 490.02904(3)(a)
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of 10 or 14 years` THEN JUST (`s 490.022(3) ends on` (`s 490.022(3) the day a number of years after the day` `the day on which the person was sentenced or found not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder, for that offence` 20))   -- paragraph 490.02904(3)(b)
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) a maximum term of life` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs 490.02904(3)(a) and (b) only are to be applied; subsection (1) is for offences none of which has a life maximum
         WHEN `s 490.022(3) any other maximum term, or none stated` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names maximum terms of two, five, 10, 14 years and life only

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029051(3) (src:10436-10437)
DECLARE `s 490.029051(3) action` IS ONE OF `s 490.029051(3) set out the duration of the obligation in the variation order`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.029051(3) (src:10436-10437)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 490.029051(3) action`
`s 490.029051(3) the duty of the court to set out the duration` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 490.029051(3) set out the duration of the obligation in the variation order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made a variation order and did not set out the duration of the obligation in it"

