    MUST `s 490.029051(5) cause the Commissioner of the Royal Canadian Mounted Police and the Attorney General of the province, or the minister of justice of the territory, in which the application for the order was made to be notified of a variation order made under this section`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court made a variation order and did not cause the notification to be given"

§ `490.02906 Appeal`

-- src:10442 | Appeal
-- src:10443 | 490.02906 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.02905(2) or (2.2) or 490.029051(2) or (3) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may
-- src:10444 | (a) dismiss the appeal; or
-- src:10445 | (b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash or amend the exemption order or variation order or make an order that may be made, as the case may be, under subsection 490.02905(2) or (2.2) or 490.029051(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02906(1) (src:10442-10445)
DECLARE `s 490.02906(1) appellant` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.02906(1) the Attorney General`
    `s 490.02906(1) the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order`
    `s 490.02906(1) another person`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02906(1) (src:10442-10445)
GIVEN appellant IS A `s 490.02906(1) appellant`
      `the decision appealed from is a decision under subsection 490.02905(2) or (2.2) or 490.029051(2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02906(1) the appeal may be brought` MEANS
    IF appellant EQUALS `s 490.02906(1) another person` OR (NOT `the decision appealed from is a decision under subsection 490.02905(2) or (2.2) or 490.029051(2) or (3)`) OR (NOT `the ground of appeal raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.02905(2) or (2.2) or 490.029051(2) or (3) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10443 | 490.02906 (1) The Attorney General or the person who applied for an exemption order or a variation order may appeal from a decision under subsection 490.02905(2) or (2.2) or 490.029051(2) or (3) on any ground of appeal that raises a question of law or of mixed law and fact. The appeal court may
-- src:10444 | (a) dismiss the appeal; or
-- src:10445 | (b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash or amend the exemption order or variation order or make an order that may be made, as the case may be, under subsection 490.02905(2) or (2.2) or 490.029051(2).
@ref Criminal Code s 490.02906(1) (src:10443-10445)
DECLARE `s 490.02906(1) thing the appeal court does` IS ONE OF
    `s 490.02906(1) dismiss the appeal`
    `s 490.02906(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing`
    `s 490.02906(1) quash the exemption order or variation order`
    `s 490.02906(1) amend the exemption order or variation order`
    `s 490.02906(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.02905(2) or (2.2) or 490.029051(2)`
    `s 490.02906(1) another thing`

@ref Criminal Code s 490.02906(1) (src:10443-10445)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 490.02906(1) thing the appeal court does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 490.02906(1) the appeal court may do it` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 490.02906(1) dismiss the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02906(1) allow the appeal and order a new hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02906(1) quash the exemption order or variation order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02906(1) amend the exemption order or variation order` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02906(1) make an order that may be made under subsection 490.02905(2) or (2.2) or 490.029051(2)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 490.02906(1) another thing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) allow the appeal and order a new hearing, quash or amend the exemption order or variation order or make an order that may be made"

